@* Sessions UI: the sessions an environment has a record of, and what an
   operator can see about them. The pane is scoped by nothing but the port it
   injects, so these imports are the module's published surface and the control
   namespaces the pane renders — no context namespace belongs here.

   Every Backlog.* import is written as @@using global::Backlog.Something. This
   project's root namespace is Backlog.Modules.Sessions.UI, and the Razor
   generator emits these directives inside that namespace without a global::
   prefix, so a bare "Backlog" would bind to Backlog.Modules the moment anything
   in this project's reference closure declares a Backlog.Modules.Backlog
   namespace. Nothing does today; global:: means nothing has to keep not doing
   it. *@
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Sessions.Abstractions
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Badges
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Buttons
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Data
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Feedback
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Integrations
